## Minimal graded resolution

The Hilbert numerator is

```text
1 - 4t^11 + t^12 + t^13 - 15t^14 - 11t^15
  + 40t^16 + 7t^17 - 18t^18 - t^19 - t^22.
```

Because `A` is Artinian over a three-variable polynomial ring, its socle
determines the last free module with a degree-three shift. The numerator and
the already minimal 30 generators then determine the middle module. The
minimal resolution is

```text
0
 -> R(-18)^18 + R(-19) + R(-22)
 -> R(-12) + R(-13) + R(-16)^40 + R(-17)^7
 -> R(-11)^4 + R(-14)^15 + R(-15)^11
 -> R
 -> A
 -> 0.
```

Its total ranks are

```text
1, 30, 49, 20.
```

The builder computes the generated ideal through degree 20 and the socle by
all three variable-multiplication maps. The independent verifier repeats this
from every archived kernel.

